      "unit_text": "Telescoping. $\\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}(b_{t+1}-b_t)=b_T-b_0$: intermediate terms cancel in pairs. Since $\\frac1{r(r+1)}=\\frac1r-\\frac1{r+1}$, $\\sum_{r=1}^{R}\\frac1{r(r+1)}=1-\\frac1{R+1}\\to1$, which is why a failure probability $\\delta'$ can be split into pieces $\\delta'/(r(r+1))$ (Module 5). Summing a Lyapunov or dissipation inequality $V(x_{t+1})-V(x_t)\\le-\\varepsilon\\|x_t\\|^2$ over $t\\lt T$ telescopes the left side, and with $V\\ge0$:",
